TOTK: NVN2 mesh shaders that output points or lines, and a point size (docs/oot-xlate.md). Seven of OoT's 854
mesh shaders (Foliage.Nin_Ounce_NVN2.bfsha) draw the grass into a shadow map of its own as points, a vertex a blade's tip:
their control section has 1 at +0x5f (vertices of a primitive; 3 everywhere else) and their SPH enables the point size
(OMAP byte 0x35 bit 3), which comes before the position in the attribute area. The entry point took every mesh shader as
triangles of position and generic attributes, so these got the point size as x, w from the index bytes and a triangle
across three unrelated blades: a wedge over the shadow map that changed every frame. MeshStage.PrimitiveVertices picks
OutputPoints / OutputLinesEXT / OutputTrianglesEXT, the index built-in and one, two or three index bytes a primitive;
MeshStage.PointSize in VertexComponents is stored as the PointSize built-in (1 for points without one). A shader of three
vertices a primitive without the point size translates as before, byte for byte.

